WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.630
Send a friend two quick voice notes.

2
00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:05.060
The first one says «je parle».

3
00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:06.880
The second: «ils parlent».

4
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.090
On paper, that's an extra N and T.

5
00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:11.440
Play them back to back.

6
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.810
Your friend can't tell which one is which.

7
00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:18.910
So why do «je parle» and «ils
parlent» sound exactly the same,

8
00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.610
when the spelling is different?

9
00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:25.320
In this mission, you'll split
«parler» into a stem and its endings.

10
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.240
Then you'll build verbs yourself,

11
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.120
dragging stem and ending chips together.

12
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.770
Your mission: crack why two different
spellings give you one single sound.
